WEBVTT

1
00:00:43.625 --> 00:00:47.916
In verses 13.25 and 13.26,

2
00:00:47.916 --> 00:00:49.791
Lord Krishna discusses alternative paths

3
00:00:49.791 --> 00:00:53.625
that lead toward liberation.

4
00:00:53.625 --> 00:00:55.208
In verse 13.25,

5
00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:58.500
He describes three primary methods,

6
00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.625
dhyana yoga, jnana yoga, and
nishkama karma yoga,

7
00:01:02.625 --> 00:01:05.958
meaning - meditation, the cultivation
of knowledge,

8
00:01:05.958 --> 00:01:09.291
and working without attachment to results.

9
00:01:09.291 --> 00:01:10.375
Through these,

10
00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:13.333
seekers can experience the Paramatma

11
00:01:13.333 --> 00:01:16.250
and attain liberation.

12
00:01:16.250 --> 00:01:19.333
In verse 13.26, Lord Krishna

13
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:20.875
assures

14
00:01:20.875 --> 00:01:21.666
that those

15
00:01:21.666 --> 00:01:23.000
who cannot follow

16
00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.833
these defined paths can also

17
00:01:26.833 --> 00:01:28.791
attain liberation simply

18
00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:32.000
by hearing about the Paramatma

19
00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:34.041
from authentic sources

20
00:01:34.041 --> 00:01:35.875
and developing faith.

21
00:01:40.625 --> 00:01:44.375
Lord Krishna in verse 13.25,

22
00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:47.916
describes three primary approaches.

23
00:01:47.916 --> 00:01:50.166
First, dhyana yoga.

24
00:01:50.166 --> 00:01:51.958
Lord Krishna says,

25
00:01:51.958 --> 00:01:57.583
“dhyanenatmani pashyanti
kechidatmanam atmana”,

26
00:01:57.583 --> 00:01:59.583
some experience the Paramatma

27
00:01:59.583 --> 00:02:01.208
through deep

28
00:02:01.208 --> 00:02:03.666
meditation.

29
00:02:03.666 --> 00:02:07.125
These yogis practise ashtanga yoga,

30
00:02:07.125 --> 00:02:09.416
focusing on controlling the mind

31
00:02:09.416 --> 00:02:11.208
and senses,

32
00:02:11.208 --> 00:02:12.125
and ultimately

33
00:02:12.125 --> 00:02:16.041
understand the Paramatma
dwelling in their hearts.

34
00:02:16.041 --> 00:02:18.250
Second, jnana yoga.

35
00:02:18.250 --> 00:02:19.416
Others

36
00:02:19.416 --> 00:02:21.333
understand the Paramatma

37
00:02:21.333 --> 00:02:23.083
through the cultivation of knowledge,

38
00:02:23.083 --> 00:02:24.166
which involves

39
00:02:24.166 --> 00:02:25.333
analysing the distinction

40
00:02:25.333 --> 00:02:28.708
between matter and soul.

41
00:02:28.708 --> 00:02:32.333
Such seekers, called sankhya yogis,

42
00:02:32.333 --> 00:02:35.583
follow the path of analytical knowledge

43
00:02:35.583 --> 00:02:38.583
and ultimately understand the Paramatma

44
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.750
by separating the soul from the body

45
00:02:40.750 --> 00:02:44.708
and experiencing it beyond material nature.

46
00:02:44.708 --> 00:02:47.791
Third, nishkama karma yoga.

47
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:49.250
A third group

48
00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.375
understands the Paramatma

49
00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:53.458
through selfless action,

50
00:02:53.458 --> 00:02:54.416
performing work

51
00:02:54.416 --> 00:02:55.666
without attachment

52
00:02:55.666 --> 00:02:58.250
to its fruits.

53
00:02:58.250 --> 00:02:59.541
These karma

54
00:02:59.541 --> 00:03:00.750
yogis

55
00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.458
fulfil their duties with dedication,

56
00:03:03.458 --> 00:03:06.500
but offer the fruits to the Paramatma,

57
00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.583
purifying their consciousness

58
00:03:08.583 --> 00:03:12.083
and ultimately understanding the Paramatma.

59
00:03:12.083 --> 00:03:14.666
Lord Krishna made clear

60
00:03:14.666 --> 00:03:17.333
that if practised sincerely,

61
00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:18.958
all these paths

62
00:03:18.958 --> 00:03:21.208
lead toward the Paramatma.

63
00:03:21.208 --> 00:03:24.333
But He does not stop there.

64
00:03:24.333 --> 00:03:28.083
In verse 13.26, He presents another powerful

65
00:03:28.083 --> 00:03:30.041
path,

66
00:03:30.041 --> 00:03:34.708
hearing about God from others, or shravana.

67
00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:38.916
He says, ‘anye tv evam ajanantah

68
00:03:38.916 --> 00:03:41.583
shrutvanyebhya upasate’,

69
00:03:41.583 --> 00:03:43.750
meaning - those not familiar

70
00:03:43.750 --> 00:03:46.833
with complex philosophical subjects

71
00:03:46.833 --> 00:03:48.416
can also

72
00:03:48.416 --> 00:03:50.375
transcend material existence

73
00:03:50.375 --> 00:03:52.583
by hearing about the Paramatma

74
00:03:52.583 --> 00:03:56.333
from others and engaging in worship.

75
00:03:56.333 --> 00:03:59.416
This method highlights the importance
of shruti-parayana,

76
00:03:59.416 --> 00:04:03.125
being devoted to hearing.

77
00:04:03.125 --> 00:04:04.541
Those dedicated to hearing

78
00:04:04.541 --> 00:04:06.625
with faith,

79
00:04:06.625 --> 00:04:08.458
even if they do not have

80
00:04:08.458 --> 00:04:11.000
profound intellectual knowledge or the capacity

81
00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.958
for deep meditation,

82
00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:15.708
their sincerity in hearing God's glories

83
00:04:15.708 --> 00:04:18.291
and engaging in worship

84
00:04:18.291 --> 00:04:20.791
purifies their hearts.

85
00:04:20.791 --> 00:04:23.250
Lord Krishna assures,

86
00:04:23.250 --> 00:04:26.916
‘te 'pi catirantyeva mrityum’,

87
00:04:26.916 --> 00:04:27.458
meaning - 

88
00:04:27.458 --> 00:04:28.625
they too cross the cycle

89
00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:31.333
of birth and death

90
00:04:31.333 --> 00:04:33.708
and attain liberation.

91
00:04:33.708 --> 00:04:35.291
This path of shravana

92
00:04:35.291 --> 00:04:36.416
is especially relevant

93
00:04:36.416 --> 00:04:38.708
in the modern world,

94
00:04:38.708 --> 00:04:42.083
where most people do not have the capacity

95
00:04:42.083 --> 00:04:43.000
for deep meditation

96
00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.500
or philosophical analysis.

97
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:47.500
Simply by hearing

98
00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.708
from authentic sources,

99
00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:50.958
through discussions on the Bhagavad

100
00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:53.875
Gita and the singing of the Lord's holy names,

101
00:04:53.875 --> 00:04:57.416
anyone can make spiritual progress

102
00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:01.000
and cross material bondage.

103
00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.041
Thus

104
00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:04.500
Lord Krishna highlights

105
00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.708
that any sincere

106
00:05:05.708 --> 00:05:09.916
path, whether meditation, knowledge, selfless

107
00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:13.916
action, or simply hearing with faith,

108
00:05:13.916 --> 00:05:16.000
when directed toward understanding
the Paramatma,

109
00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.041
leads to liberation.

110
00:05:24.708 --> 00:05:26.333
Have you ever tried

111
00:05:26.333 --> 00:05:29.375
to pursue something

112
00:05:29.375 --> 00:05:31.833
about which you had no knowledge?

113
00:05:31.833 --> 00:05:36.083
Never. Because your thoughts
move in the direction

114
00:05:36.083 --> 00:05:40.375
of what you have already heard about.

115
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:46.083
That is why in spiritual life, shravana, hearing,

116
00:05:46.083 --> 00:05:49.458
is the most important first step.

117
00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:52.791
Even if you cannot meditate deeply

118
00:05:52.791 --> 00:05:56.291
or engage in philosophical analysis,

119
00:05:56.291 --> 00:05:57.708
you can still

120
00:05:57.708 --> 00:05:59.250
move forward simply by hearing

121
00:05:59.250 --> 00:06:02.500
from the right source.

122
00:06:02.500 --> 00:06:04.125
Because what you hear

123
00:06:04.125 --> 00:06:09.208
shapes the way you think,

124
00:06:09.208 --> 00:06:12.833
and from that flows the way you live.

125
00:06:12.833 --> 00:06:14.583
For example,

126
00:06:14.583 --> 00:06:17.291
if you must travel through

127
00:06:17.291 --> 00:06:20.208
an unfamiliar forest path,

128
00:06:20.208 --> 00:06:22.833
you ask experienced travellers

129
00:06:22.833 --> 00:06:24.916
before entering.

130
00:06:24.916 --> 00:06:27.208
Otherwise the chances of getting lost

131
00:06:27.208 --> 00:06:29.458
or into danger

132
00:06:29.458 --> 00:06:31.458
are very high.

133
00:06:31.458 --> 00:06:35.000
The inner world cannot be improved

134
00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.833
by guesswork alone.

135
00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:39.875
For this, you need knowledge

136
00:06:39.875 --> 00:06:43.916
that goes beyond your present thinking,

137
00:06:43.916 --> 00:06:47.875
and that comes through shravana, hearing.

138
00:06:47.875 --> 00:06:50.291
So understand deeply the importance

139
00:06:50.291 --> 00:06:53.833
of sitting in a Gita class, listening to
a wise teacher,

140
00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:57.833
or hearing a spiritual talk

141
00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:01.041
while travelling.

142
00:07:01.041 --> 00:07:03.500
If the source is authentic

143
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:08.333
and your heart is open, this one act

144
00:07:08.333 --> 00:07:10.000
of listening

145
00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.583
becomes the first link

146
00:07:11.583 --> 00:07:15.416
in the chain of change in your life.

147
00:07:15.416 --> 00:07:19.875
Because hearing leads to knowing,

148
00:07:19.875 --> 00:07:22.833
and knowing leads to building.

149
00:07:22.833 --> 00:07:27.000
This is where the journey begins,

150
00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:31.375
the journey of shaping your spiritual self.

151
00:07:36.083 --> 00:07:37.583
There are many paths

152
00:07:37.583 --> 00:07:40.625
to spiritual progress,

153
00:07:40.625 --> 00:07:43.291
meditation, selfless action,

154
00:07:43.291 --> 00:07:46.291
or philosophical study.

155
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:49.000
But in today's busy world,

156
00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:50.333
one of the simplest

157
00:07:50.333 --> 00:07:53.666
and most effective means is,

158
00:07:53.666 --> 00:07:57.791
shravana, hearing.

159
00:07:57.791 --> 00:07:59.833
Even if it is only

160
00:07:59.833 --> 00:08:03.833
that all the members of the family sit together

161
00:08:03.833 --> 00:08:08.166
and listen to spiritual discussions,
stories, or verses from the Gita,

162
00:08:08.166 --> 00:08:15.291
this can begin a quiet and
beautiful transformation.

163
00:08:15.291 --> 00:08:17.666
Those who are not greatly learned,

164
00:08:17.666 --> 00:08:20.875
scholarly, or meditative

165
00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:23.625
can also reach Me simply by hearing

166
00:08:23.625 --> 00:08:26.083
from the right people

167
00:08:26.083 --> 00:08:28.875
with faith.

168
00:08:28.875 --> 00:08:32.000
Think about what a joyful change

169
00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:35.083
this would be for your family!

170
00:08:35.083 --> 00:08:38.291
A small daily practice,

171
00:08:38.291 --> 00:08:41.708
sitting together to hear a brief talk,

172
00:08:41.708 --> 00:08:43.666
a spiritual story,

173
00:08:43.666 --> 00:08:47.000
or the meaning of a verse,

174
00:08:47.000 --> 00:08:49.708
becomes a thread that connects

175
00:08:49.708 --> 00:08:51.875
the hearts of family members.

176
00:08:51.875 --> 00:08:53.500
This is not about

177
00:08:53.500 --> 00:08:56.916
giving advice or imposing your views.

178
00:08:56.916 --> 00:09:00.416
It is simply letting knowledge flow gently

179
00:09:00.416 --> 00:09:03.625
into the atmosphere of the home.

180
00:09:03.625 --> 00:09:06.291
It dissolves ego,

181
00:09:06.291 --> 00:09:08.166
calms restlessness,

182
00:09:08.166 --> 00:09:12.166
and makes the home a sacred space.

183
00:09:12.166 --> 00:09:13.875
If you want

184
00:09:13.875 --> 00:09:17.875
your family to grow together, not just outwardly

185
00:09:17.875 --> 00:09:21.666
but inwardly,

186
00:09:21.666 --> 00:09:25.166
create a culture of shravana.

187
00:09:25.166 --> 00:09:28.125
Not just listening to each other,

188
00:09:28.125 --> 00:09:31.916
but listening together

189
00:09:31.916 --> 00:09:35.625
to what truly matters.

190
00:09:35.625 --> 00:09:39.458
This shared journey becomes the foundation

191
00:09:39.458 --> 00:09:43.041
of lasting peace and mutual connection.

192
00:09:47.916 --> 00:09:52.500
The best learning comes from experience.

193
00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:54.708
In professional life,

194
00:09:54.708 --> 00:09:57.750
you often hear this.

195
00:09:57.750 --> 00:10:01.583
It is true. But also know

196
00:10:01.583 --> 00:10:05.458
that experience is an expensive teacher,

197
00:10:05.458 --> 00:10:09.375
it sometimes means being wrong

198
00:10:09.375 --> 00:10:14.333
and failing.

199
00:10:14.333 --> 00:10:18.083
How good it would be if instead of

200
00:10:18.083 --> 00:10:20.666
this hard path of learning,

201
00:10:20.666 --> 00:10:25.375
you found a simpler way?

202
00:10:25.375 --> 00:10:27.166
That simpler way

203
00:10:27.166 --> 00:10:30.125
is described in this verse.

204
00:10:30.125 --> 00:10:34.125
Shravana, understand it well.

205
00:10:34.125 --> 00:10:38.500
You do not always need to figure out

206
00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:42.375
and test everything yourself.

207
00:10:42.375 --> 00:10:45.750
When you listen with respect and

208
00:10:45.750 --> 00:10:47.708
attention

209
00:10:47.708 --> 00:10:50.875
to those who have walked that path before,

210
00:10:50.875 --> 00:10:53.250
teachers, experienced leaders,

211
00:10:53.250 --> 00:10:57.083
or eternal teachings like the Gita,

212
00:10:57.083 --> 00:10:58.041
you begin

213
00:10:58.041 --> 00:11:02.375
from a much better place.

214
00:11:02.375 --> 00:11:06.958
Shravana gives you perspectives

215
00:11:06.958 --> 00:11:12.500
you may never have reached on your own.

216
00:11:12.500 --> 00:11:14.291
For example,

217
00:11:14.291 --> 00:11:17.583
if you are given responsibility

218
00:11:17.583 --> 00:11:19.083
for an unfamiliar

219
00:11:19.083 --> 00:11:22.083
machine at work,

220
00:11:22.083 --> 00:11:25.125
learning to operate it entirely on your own

221
00:11:25.125 --> 00:11:29.375
would take a very long time.

222
00:11:29.375 --> 00:11:31.041
What would you do?

223
00:11:31.041 --> 00:11:33.916
Try to figure it out alone,

224
00:11:33.916 --> 00:11:40.916
or seek help from someone with experience?

225
00:11:40.916 --> 00:11:44.333
Clearly, talking to experienced people

226
00:11:44.333 --> 00:11:46.541
will make you skilled

227
00:11:46.541 --> 00:11:50.083
in far less time.

228
00:11:50.083 --> 00:11:54.791
In today's world, 'doing'

229
00:11:54.791 --> 00:11:57.458
is considered a great achievement,

230
00:11:57.458 --> 00:12:01.708
while the skill of listening is undervalued.

231
00:12:01.708 --> 00:12:03.166
But real learning

232
00:12:03.166 --> 00:12:06.291
begins right there.

233
00:12:06.291 --> 00:12:08.583
It makes you humble and clear

234
00:12:08.583 --> 00:12:10.625
in thinking.

235
00:12:10.625 --> 00:12:14.166
It prepares you to respond thoughtfully

236
00:12:14.166 --> 00:12:17.541
and calmly rather than

237
00:12:17.541 --> 00:12:19.541
reacting instantly.

238
00:12:19.541 --> 00:12:20.333
This humble

239
00:12:20.333 --> 00:12:24.416
spirit of learning takes you toward the finest

240
00:12:24.416 --> 00:12:28.125
path of knowledge,

241
00:12:28.125 --> 00:12:31.458
which may be the wisdom already

242
00:12:31.458 --> 00:12:34.500
gathered by someone experienced.

243
00:12:34.500 --> 00:12:39.708
So let knowledge be your guide,

244
00:12:39.708 --> 00:12:43.083
quietly, but powerfully.
